    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG O'Sullivan Hurley are delighted to welcome this detached property to the market for sale by online public auction (unless previously sold) on Friday 16th October 2026 at 12pm.\n\nTo access legal documents and to register to bid please use the following link; \nhttps://osullivanhurley.dngauctions.ie/lot/details/2c737f37-997f-4c79-bc9d-13b7e10aefe5\n\nLocated just two kilometres north of Crusheen village just off the Tubber road on a quiet cul de sac road is this splendid three bedroom detached cottage set on an incredible site of approximately 0.7 acres. The Burren National Park and Wild Atlantic Way are just twenty minutes, Ennis town centre fifteen minutes and ease of access to the M18 motorway for those commuting to Shannon/Limerick/Galway and with all the amenities in Crusheen village just a few minutes by car. Ideal for the first time buyer or family home buyer with the cottage offering outstanding potential to be extended subject to the relevant planning and qualifying for the valuable refurbishment grants subject to terms and conditions. All accommodation is set at ground floor level, with entrance porchway, open plan kitchen/living/dining and three bedrooms. Viewing is highly recommended and strictly by prior appointment with sole selling agents. PSL 002295"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch - 1.7m x 1.65m\nDoor leading to open plan kitchen/living/dining.\n\nKitchen/Living/Dining - 4.23m x 3.8m\nSolid fuel range and connecting doors to bedrooms one, two and three.\n\nBedroom One - 3.15m x 2m\n\n\nBedroom Two - 2.9m x 2m\n\n\nBedroom Three - 4.4m x 2.7m\n\n\n"
      },
